# Line endings — this file exists because Forge is edited on Windows and run on Linux.
#
# THE PROBLEM
# Windows ends lines with CRLF (\r\n); Linux and macOS use LF (\n). Git for
# Windows defaults to core.autocrlf=true, which converts LF to CRLF when it
# writes files into your working directory and back to LF when you commit.
# That works fine for prose and mostly fine for code — but it breaks two things
# badly, and both live in this repo:
#
#   1. Shell scripts. The kernel reads the shebang line literally, so a stray
#      \r makes the interpreter path "/usr/bin/env bash\r", which does not
#      exist. The error is the famous and completely unhelpful:
#          bash: ./forge: /usr/bin/env: bad interpreter: No such file or directory
#      ...where the ^M is invisible in most editors. Hours have been lost to it.
#
#   2. Any file a checker compares byte-for-byte. Forge's lesson checkers
#      compare exact output; a trailing \r on a line silently fails a correct
#      answer.
#
# THE FIX
# `text=auto eol=lf` tells git: detect which files are text, and always write
# LF into the working directory regardless of platform. It overrides
# core.autocrlf, so it protects everyone who clones this repo without each of
# them having to configure anything.
#
# If a file already went wrong, `git add --renormalize .` re-applies these
# rules to the whole tree.

* text=auto eol=lf

# Belt and braces for the files where a CRLF is actually fatal.
*.sh      text eol=lf
*.mjs     text eol=lf
*.js      text eol=lf
*.jsx     text eol=lf
*.json    text eol=lf
*.yml     text eol=lf
forge     text eol=lf

# Binary files must never be touched by line-ending conversion — "fixing"
# line endings inside a PNG corrupts it.
*.png     binary
*.jpg     binary
*.ico     binary
*.gz      binary

# Generated files. `linguist-generated` collapses them in GitHub's diff view
# and keeps them out of the repository's language statistics, so the language
# bar reflects code you wrote rather than a 3MB generated index.
docs/CURRICULUM.md  linguist-generated=true
package-lock.json   linguist-generated=true
